30,2,,status,Minako,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":1,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
31,2,,status,Yumi,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":2,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
32,2,,status,Benjamin,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":3,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
33,2,,status,Daisuke,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":4,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
34,2,,status,Shion,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":5,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
35,2,1,talk,Yumi,,"It's worrying! I found out that two outer wards lost their bus links, so people there have to travel an hour just to reach us. And the road closures north of the river happened eleven days last winter.","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Benjamin,,"That is quite a revelation, Yumi. Interestingly, my research shows that former outreach stops in those outer wards actually drew more visitors per session than the main building does midweek.","{""words"":30,""mentions"":[""Yumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,Shion,,"I found that we have retired tradespeople volunteering for repairs, but no one on the payroll is actually trained to supervise outside facilitators. Also, our power tool certification technician retired in spring.","{""words"":32,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Minako,,"My findings show that the county grant only covers session fees for the first year, after which the operating budget takes over. Also, last year's vehicle running costs overran by a third.","{""words"":32,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Daisuke,,"I also saw that the bus links are gone, like Yumi said. And... the evening room bookings are full, but people are using the catalogue from home long after we've locked up.","{""words"":32,""mentions"":[""Yumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Yumi,,"That's so sad that people are stuck at home! If the bus links are gone and the roads close, we really need to find a way to bring the library to them, don't you think?","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Benjamin,,"While the sentiment is noble, Yumi, we must consider the historical data. My research indicates that outreach was successful, but we should be cautious about repeating past failures.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[""Yumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,Shion,,"Exactly. If we don't have the staff to supervise specialized equipment or facilitators, some of these ""noble"" ideas will just be liabilities. We can't ignore the skill gap.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Minako,,"We must also consider the financial structure. If the grant only covers the first year, we risk a budget shortfall in the second year, especially if vehicle costs continue to overrun.","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Daisuke,,"I... I agree with Minako. If we start something that costs too much to keep running, we might have to stop it just when people finally start relying on it.","{""words"":30,""mentions"":[""Minako""],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Yumi,,"But we can't just do nothing while people are cut off! @Benjamin, you said outreach worked before, so maybe we can find a way to make it sustainable this time?","{""words"":30,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Benjamin,,"I am open to the possibility, Yumi, provided we analyze why the previous funding lapsed. We must ensure the model is logically sound before we commit.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Yumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,Shion,,"Regardless of the model, if we lack the certified staff to manage the service, it's a non-starter. We can't just wish expertise into existence.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,Minako,,"We must be pragmatic. If we choose a service that requires specialized certification or high vehicle maintenance, we need a funding plan that extends beyond the first year's grant.","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Daisuke,,"I wonder if something that doesn't require a vehicle or special certification would be safer, since people are already using the catalogue from home so much.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,4,talk,Yumi,,"That's a good point, Daisuke! But if people are already using the catalogue from home, maybe we can give them even more tools to learn and grow without needing to travel?","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[""Daisuke""],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,4,talk,Benjamin,,"That is a logical pivot. If we can provide value remotely or through existing community structures, we avoid the logistical pitfalls Yumi and Daisuke highlighted.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Yumi"",""Daisuke""],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,4,talk,Shion,,"As long as it doesn't require us to hire a whole new team of specialists we can't afford or supervise, I'm on board with a more streamlined approach.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,2,4,talk,Minako,,I agree. We must prioritize a proposal that balances community need with our actual capacity for long-term financial and operational maintenance.,"{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,2,4,talk,Daisuke,,"I just hope we pick something that doesn't leave anyone behind, even if it's not the most ambitious plan.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
