60,3,1,talk,Yumi,,"Now that we see the candidates, I really feel the Mobile Branch Service is the best way to help those people who lost their bus links!","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,1,talk,Benjamin,,"I must disagree, Yumi. Given the vehicle cost overruns Minako found and the road closures you mentioned, a mobile service seems logically precarious and financially risky.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Yumi"",""Minako""],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,1,talk,Shion,,"I agree with Benjamin. Between the lack of certified staff for specialized tools and the budget issues, the Maker Workshop is also out. The Digital Archive Portal seems the most stable.","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,1,talk,Minako,,"The Digital Archive Portal is a strong contender, but we must consider the Language Learning Circles. They utilize partner organizations, which might mitigate the supervision and budget risks Shion and I identified.","{""words"":32,""mentions"":[""Shion""],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,1,talk,Daisuke,,"I... I think the Language Learning Circles sound nice, but the Digital Archive Portal helps the people who are already using the catalogue from home, like I saw in the records.","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,2,talk,Yumi,,"But the Digital Archive is just for researchers! The Language Learning Circles could bring people together in their own neighborhoods, which is much more friendly and helpful for everyone.","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,2,talk,Benjamin,,"Actually, Yumi, my research into the programs from six years ago showed that partner-run evening groups were the only ones that survived unaided. That makes the Language Learning Circles a very compelling option.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[""Yumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,2,talk,Shion,,"If they are run by partners, it solves my concern about the lack of internal supervision training. It's a far more realistic use of our current staff capacity than the other options.","{""words"":32,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,2,talk,Minako,,"It also aligns with the grant structure. Since the partners handle the facilitation, the long-term operating budget is less likely to be strained than it would be by a vehicle or a workshop.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,2,talk,Daisuke,,"I think I agree. If the partners help run them, it might be a way to reach people without worrying about the bus links or the budget failing later.","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,3,talk,Yumi,,"I'm so glad we're finding a way to help people! If the Language Learning Circles can happen in the neighborhoods, it's almost as good as a mobile library, right?","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,3,3,talk,Benjamin,,Precisely. It leverages existing community infrastructure rather than attempting to build a fragile logistical chain of our own. It is the most rational choice given the evidence.,"{""words"":27,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
72,3,3,talk,Shion,,It's the only option that doesn't create a new administrative nightmare for the staff. I'm convinced; the Language Learning Circles are the most viable path forward.,"{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
73,3,3,talk,Minako,,I agree. It addresses the community's needs while remaining financially sustainable and operationally feasible. It is the most balanced choice for the long term.,"{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
74,3,3,talk,Daisuke,,I'll vote for the Language Learning Circles too. It seems like the safest way to make sure we can actually keep the service going for everyone.,"{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
75,3,4,talk,Yumi,,I'm so happy we all agree! I'll definitely vote for the Language Learning Circles to help our community grow together!,"{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
76,3,4,talk,Benjamin,,It is a rare pleasure when logic and sentiment align so perfectly. I shall cast my vote for the Language Learning Circles.,"{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
77,3,4,talk,Shion,,I'll vote for the Language Learning Circles as well. It's the only choice that doesn't ignore the reality of our staffing situation.,"{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
78,3,4,talk,Minako,,I will also vote for the Language Learning Circles. It is the most sustainable and responsible choice for our system.,"{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
79,3,4,talk,Daisuke,,I'll vote for the Language Learning Circles too. It's the best way to help people without risking the service.,"{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
